{
  "name": "workspace-checkpoint-list-names-who-registered",
  "description": "#191 provenance over the wire: A takes a checkpoint naming B as receiver; B registers a restore of it. The listing then carries three DIFFERENT controller ids -- `owner` A, `receiver` B, `registered_by` B -- each preserved verbatim, so a row that credited the registration to A (the owner, which a pre-#191 reading might assume) fails. `owner` is provenance and is never compared to the registering controller.",
